From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:01:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] renderer: the caller's planes of the Dolby Vision composer
 may be of 16 bits

pl_render_params.dovi_ccm_planes (libplacebo-9932) has the composer of
ETSI GS CCM 001 write the composed planes into textures of the caller's,
which must be of the formats the composer picks: 32-bit floats (R32F for
the luma, RG32F for the chroma). With dovi_ccm_only nothing in the render
reads them afterwards: they are the caller's, and a caller that sends the
composed picture (Kodi's source transport of Dolby Vision) reads only the
codes from them. A sample is h / 2^hdr_bit_depth, h a code of at most 12
bits; in a 16-bit normalized texture it is stored as that times 65535 to
within half a step, or a step where a GPU truncates, which is less than
1/16 of a code: the caller reads the code back exactly as
round(stored * 2^hdr_bit_depth), from half the bytes (for a 3840x2160
picture 24.9 MB written and read instead of 49.8).

With dovi_ccm_only the caller's textures may now be of 16-bit normalized
formats (PL_FMT_UNORM, 16 bits, 1 component for the luma, 2 for the
chroma; renderable and sampleable as before) where hdr_bit_depth is 12 or
less. PL_DOVI_CCM_PLANES_UNORM16 says that the renderer takes them.
Without dovi_ccm_only, or for 32-bit textures, nothing changes.

Measured on Mesa's software OpenGL ES (zink on lavapipe) with Kodi's Dolby
Vision bridge, which takes R16 and RG16 where the GPU renders to them: the
codes read back from the 16-bit planes are those of the 32-bit ones in
every sample, and every transport the same bytes (see the bridge's
commit).

License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, that of libplacebo and of the files changed,
whose notices stay as they are.
---
 src/include/libplacebo/renderer.h | 12 ++++++++++++
 src/renderer.c                    | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/include/libplacebo/renderer.h b/src/include/libplacebo/renderer.h
index 52295cfe..ffcb6cb5 100644
--- a/src/include/libplacebo/renderer.h
+++ b/src/include/libplacebo/renderer.h
@@ -145,6 +145,9 @@ struct pl_render_info {
 
 // Represents the options used for rendering. These affect the quality of
 // the result.
+// Hades: `pl_render_params.dovi_ccm_planes` may be of 16-bit normalized formats
+#define PL_DOVI_CCM_PLANES_UNORM16 1
+
 struct pl_render_params {
     // Configures the algorithms used for upscaling and downscaling,
     // respectively. If left as NULL, then libplacebo will only use inexpensive
@@ -422,6 +425,15 @@ struct pl_render_params {
     // from them as from its own. `dovi_ccm_composed`, when set, says whether
     // the image was composed into them. Textures that do not fit are a reason
     // not to compose the image so, logged as the others. Hades extension.
+    //
+    // With `dovi_ccm_only` (below) they may instead be of 16-bit normalized
+    // formats (PL_FMT_UNORM, 16 bits, 1 and 2 components), renderable and
+    // sampleable: a sample h / 2^hdr_bit_depth (hdr_bit_depth at most 12) is
+    // stored as h / 2^hdr_bit_depth * 65535 to within half a step or one
+    // step, whichever way the GPU rounds, which is less than 1/16 of h's step
+    // apart: the caller reads h back exactly as round(stored * 2^depth), from
+    // half the bytes. Nothing in the render reads them then.
+    // (PL_DOVI_CCM_PLANES_UNORM16)
     pl_tex dovi_ccm_planes[2];
     bool *dovi_ccm_composed;
 
diff --git a/src/renderer.c b/src/renderer.c
index 69097244..54ddcd32 100644
--- a/src/renderer.c
+++ b/src/renderer.c
@@ -2057,6 +2057,18 @@ static pl_shader ccm_begin(struct pass_state *pass, int w, int h,
 }
 
 // (into `dst`, a texture of the caller's that ccm_check() found fit, when given)
+// Hades: a 16-bit normalized format of n components, every one 16 bits
+static bool unorm16(pl_fmt fmt, int n)
+{
+    if (!fmt || fmt->type != PL_FMT_UNORM || fmt->num_components != n)
+        return false;
+    for (int c = 0; c < n; c++) {
+        if (fmt->component_depth[c] != 16)
+            return false;
+    }
+    return true;
+}
+
 static pl_tex ccm_end(struct pass_state *pass, pl_shader sh, pl_fmt fmt,
                       int w, int h, pl_tex dst)
 {
@@ -2680,7 +2692,12 @@ static const char *ccm_check(struct pass_state *pass, struct ccm_ctx *x)
     if (dl || dc || params->dovi_ccm_only) {
         if (!dl || !dc)
             return "a texture of the caller's for one of the composed planes only";
-        if (dl->params.format != x->fmt1 || dc->params.format != x->fmt2 ||
+        // (Hades: or, where nothing else is drawn, in 16-bit normalized
+        // formats, which hold every code of hdr_bit_depth bits exactly
+        // enough to be read back: see `dovi_ccm_planes`)
+        const bool norm16 = params->dovi_ccm_only && pp->hdr_depth <= 12 &&
+                            unorm16(dl->params.format, 1) && unorm16(dc->params.format, 2);
+        if ((!norm16 && (dl->params.format != x->fmt1 || dc->params.format != x->fmt2)) ||
             !dl->params.renderable || !dl->params.sampleable ||
             !dc->params.renderable || !dc->params.sampleable)
             return "the caller's textures for the composed planes are not of the composer's formats";
